LBM source provenance

The original LBM layout, macros, grid utilities, and numerical cell body are
from wsmoses/Enzyme-GPU-Tests (LBM), derived from the University of Illinois
benchmark code. Their copyright notices are retained:

(C) Copyright 2010 The Board of Trustees of the University of Illinois
All Rights Reserved

The spatial and temporal experiments were extracted from the local opt-c,
opt-d128, opt-d128-2, opt-c128, opt-c128-2, opt-3044 and opt-3044-2 work.
The common collision body is copied without expression changes. Temporal
tile sizes are template parameters; debug-only instrumentation is omitted.
The standalone launch registry, experiment scripts and documentation were
assembled for this repository. See docs/provenance.json for exact source
paths and hashes, including local changes beyond the upstream commit.

No repository-wide license text for these LBM sources was present in the
inspected source snapshot. This extraction does not assign a new blanket
license to the imported code. The upstream project is:
https://github.com/wsmoses/Enzyme-GPU-Tests
